Article 19. Where the luggage and articles kept by a tourism business operator or tourism auxiliary service provider on behalf of a tourist are damaged or lost, and the tourist requests compensation for losses, the People's Court shall support the request, except in the following circumstances:
(1) the loss is caused by the tourist's failure to carry cash, securities, or valuables with him or her, contrary to the prior declaration or notice of the tourism business operator or tourism auxiliary service provider;
(2) the loss is caused by force majeure;
(3) the loss is caused by the tourist's fault;
(4) the loss is caused by the natural properties of the articles.

Article 20. Where a tourist requests the tourism business operator to refund the following expenses, the People's Court shall support the request:
(1) expenses additionally charged for refusing shopping activities arranged by the tourism business operator or separately paid items;
(2) expenses additionally charged in the same tourism itinerary due to differences in the tourist's age, occupation, etc., where the tourism business operator provides the same services.
